<BlogLayout
  title="Why MEP Retrofits Live or Die on the Existing-Conditions Scan"
  description="MEP coordination in an existing building is only as good as the as-built it's based on. Here's why laser scanning above the ceiling is the highest-value scan on most retrofit projects."
  category="Guide"
  readTime="7 min"
>
  <p>The most expensive surprises in construction almost always live above the ceiling. A mechanical contractor routes a new duct exactly where the drawings said there was clear space, and finds an existing beam, a sprinkler main, and a conduit run already occupying it. Now there's an RFI, a delay, and a change order. Multiply that across a retrofit and the numbers get serious fast.</p>

